# Documentation Website (`www/docs/`)

Refer to [Astro/Starlight](https://docs.vlt.sh) for code blocks, components and front end config.


## Content Structure

```
www/docs/src/content/docs/
├── get-started/            # Intro, use cases, npm interop
│   └── concepts/           # Core concepts (dependencies, manifests, registries)
├── cli/                    # CLI reference (options, guides)
│   ├── commands/           # Per-command docs
│   ├── migration/          # Migration guides from npm/pnpm/yarn
│   └── selectors/          # DSS selector reference (pseudo-classes, combinators, etc.)
├── registry/               # vlt registry docs (publishing, tokens, dashboard)
├── packages/               # Package API docs (auto-generated)
├── feedback/               # Feedback page
└── index.mdx               # Site homepage
```

## Format

MDX files with Astro/Starlight components. Frontmatter:
```mdx
---
title: Page Title
sidebar:
  label: Short Label
  order: 1
---
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components'
```

Use `<Code code="..." title="Terminal" lang="bash" />` for command examples.

## When to Update Docs

- Adding/changing CLI options → update `cli/configuring.mdx`
- Adding/changing commands → update/create `cli/commands/<cmd>.mdx`
- Adding DSS selectors → update `cli/selectors/` (index + new files)
- Changing install/build behavior → update relevant command + concept docs

## Dev

```bash
cd www/docs
pnpm dev    # local dev server
pnpm build  # production build
```

## Deployment (Vercel)

`www/docs` uses `output: 'server'` with the `@astrojs/vercel` adapter,
which emits Vercel's Build Output API v3 (`www/docs/.vercel/output/`) —
this includes both the static assets **and** the `_render` serverless
function plus `config.json` routing rules that make dynamic/SSR routes
(e.g. `src/pages/api/**`) work.

**Never set an `outputDirectory` for this project** — not in the root
`vercel.json`, and not in the Vercel dashboard's Framework Settings.
Pointing `outputDirectory` at `www/docs/dist` or even
`www/docs/.vercel/output/static` makes Vercel deploy only that static
folder as a plain static site, silently dropping the adapter's
serverless function and routing config. Symptoms: static pages still
render fine, but any SSR/API route (`/api/markdown/*`, `/_image`, etc.)
404s at the Vercel platform level (`x-vercel-error: NOT_FOUND`), and if
`outputDirectory` points above `.vercel/output/static`, pages can end
up served from an unexpected subpath (e.g. `/client/`).

Vercel should auto-detect `.vercel/output` produced by the adapter —
leave Output Directory unset/default in both `vercel.json` and the
dashboard.
